  "scope": "Same 12 lexical identities, senses and 15 padas as PG206. These three lakāras supply 405 previously unwritten keys for that grid. Each 3sg/dual/plural luṭ series uses the special third-person substitutes under 2.4.85.",
  "history": "Retain the root citation, lexical class, pada, original accent/iṭ entitlement, causative suffix if inherent, outer sya versus tās, and the conditional aṭ. The two present-system factors śap and śyan do not precede the future suffixes. Curādi ṇic remains part of its derived root. iṭ entitlement is queried on that underlying root history.",
  "ashtadhyayi_decisions": {
    "7.2.10 and 7.2.35": "Three aniṭ root identities (both styai and nam) exclude iṭ under the selected single-vowel unaccented-upadeśa condition. The nine other roots use seṭ on these requests.",
    "3.1.33": "tāsi for luṭ; sya for lṛṭ and lṛṅ. No śap or śyan inserted between these future affixes and the root.",
    "6.4.71": "Only the conditional receives aṭ. All twelve roots are consonant-initial.",
    "8.3.24 and 8.4.58": "Nam produces nantā before t and naṃsyati before s. When iṭ is present on sam, the root m faces a vowel, yielding samitā, samiṣyati."
  },
